<title>INDONESIA: TABLE-Bank Int'l Indonesia H1 net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Bank Int'l Indonesia H1 net up.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			 (in billion rupiah except per share)</p>
<p>    Net income			201.62	 vs    146.15</p>
<p>    Net interest income	   371.43	 vs    303.73</p>
<p>    Earnings per share  (rph)    72	    vs     76</p>
<p>    Other operating income	120.40	 vs    101.43</p>
<p>    Operating profit		258.30	 vs    215.98</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  268.75	 vs    209.87</p>
<p>    Retained earnings	     465.50	 vs    150.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The results were consolidated.  PT Bank Internasional Indonesia, a member of the Sinar Mas Group conglomerate, is among the largest privately-owned banks in Indonesia.</p>
